    "citeAs": "Dornelas M, Antão LH, Moyes F, Bates, AE, Magurran, AE, et al. BioTIME: A database of biodiversity time series for the Anthropocene. Global Ecol Biogeogr. 2018; 27:760 - 786. https://doi.org/10.1111/geb.12729",
    "description": "The BioTIME database contains raw data on species identities and abundances within ecological communities tracked through time. It consists of a main raw data table and several related metadata tables that provide detailed information about the studies included. The data allows researchers to analyze changes in biodiversity and species composition across various ecosystems globally. The dataset is provided in multiple formats to facilitate use, including an SQL file for importing into databases, large CSV files for data analysis, metadata files describing the studies, and citation lists for proper acknowledgment. Additionally, an R Markdown document offers guidance on interacting with the data programmatically.",
